// Expect CatalogReadsCorrect to fail: GC of a sqlite_schema version ignores the
// floor, and the generation gate stays on. A DROP commits without a
// generation bump. Only the publish that destroys the table bumps it, and the
// reader compiles before that publish. The reader begins after the DROP with
// a mark below the frame that destroys the table, and GC drops the chain. The reader's B-tree still has
// the table. MaxTs = 3 is too small for this.
